        "methodological_differences": {
            "1_raw_table5_replication_and_table6_srp_subtraction": "Before subtracting non-EP synodic offsets, Ke et al. (2026, Table 5) independently detect a significant negative cos(D) residual in INPOP21 (-2.328 +/- 0.314 mm at 7.41 sigma on ALL 1970-2024; -2.414 +/- 0.315 mm at 7.66 sigma on OCA 1984-2024; -2.629 +/- 0.831 mm on OCA 1984-2016; -2.450 +/- 0.716 mm at 3.42 sigma on APOLLO 2006-2024; -3.052 +/- 1.106 mm on APOLLO 2006-2016) and DE430 (-2.612 +/- 0.671 mm at 3.89 sigma on ALL 1970-2016), replicating the negative post-fit synodic sign. After dividing by their span- and station-specific WLS recovery factors K_eff (0.740 on ALL 1970-2024, 0.690 on ALL 1970-2016, 0.874 on OCA 1984-2024, 0.790 on OCA 1984-2016, 0.560 on APOLLO 2006-2024, and 0.610 on APOLLO 2006-2016), their attenuation-corrected pre-SRP/thermal amplitudes are -3.146 mm (INPOP21 ALL 1970-2024), -3.446 mm (INPOP21 ALL 1970-2016), -3.786 mm (DE430 ALL 1970-2016), -3.328 mm (INPOP21 OCA 1984-2016), -4.375 mm (INPOP21 APOLLO 2006-2024 and DE430 APOLLO 2006-2016), and -5.003 mm (INPOP21 APOLLO 2006-2016). Their Table 6 nulls (-0.146 +/- 1.066 mm on INPOP21 ALL and -0.786 +/- 2.074 mm on DE430 ALL; -1.375 to -2.003 mm on APOLLO) follow from adding the +3.00 +/- 0.50 mm orbital-SRP + retroreflector-thermal correction and scaling formal WLS uncertainties by 3x in quadrature with 0.50 mm.",
